{"reference":"Proverbs 14","book":"Proverbs","chapter":14,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Wealth, Poverty, and Justice","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Proverbs 14:31 should keep readers from treating the chapter’s sayings about labor and material outcomes as simple explanations for every person’s condition. Proverbs connects some outcomes with diligence and choice, but it also condemns oppression of the poor and other forms of unjust dealing. Here, mercy toward the needy is presented as honoring their Maker.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 14:31"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_014_9792171c781b38b7f4290602"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}